A factory makes boots and sandals. The number made in any week of

\begin{itemize}
\item boots and sandals is a total of 200
\item boots is a maximum of 120
\item sandals is a maximum of 150
\end{itemize}

The factory manager has drawn a graph to show the number of pairs of boots ($x$) and sandals ($y$) that can be made.

\exfigure{1228_q11_1}

The graph shows both the theoretical power generated and the actual power generated by a particular wind turbine.

\exfigure{1228_q13_2}

Using the graph, or otherwise, find the difference between the theoretical power and the actual power generated when the wind speed is 9 m/s.
